{#
  T-3.04 — the header, transparent over the hero.

  | Variable         | Type    | Description                     |
  |------------------|---------|---------------------------------|
  | cart             | object  |                                 |
  | cart.items_count | int     |                                 |
  | cart.total       | string  | Formatted total ex: "١٠٠ ر.س"   |

  ONE BAR, NOT TWO. Upstream ships a top navbar above the main nav carrying the
  footer menu, the language/currency switcher, the store scope and an inline
  search field. **No artboard draws any of it.** The design's header is a single
  row: burger and search at the start, the wordmark centred, cart and avatar at
  the end. The top navbar is removed rather than hidden, and the two things in it
  that are functionality rather than decoration — `salla-localization-modal` and
  `salla-contacts` — are CARRIED TO T-3.06, which owns the burger menu and is the
  place they belong. That carry is recorded in the backlog; they are not deleted.

  ORDER IS RTL ORDER. In an RTL row the first child sits on the right. So the DOM
  reads burger → search → wordmark → cart → avatar, which renders right-to-left
  exactly as the artboard draws it. Reversing the two groups to "fix" the visual
  order on an LTR store would break the RTL one; the flex direction handles it.

  THE SKIP LINK LIVES HERE. `master.twig` includes this component immediately
  after the `body:start` hook, so the link below is the first focusable thing on
  the page — which is the only property that makes a skip link a skip link. It
  targets `#main-content`, the id `master.twig` already gives its `<main>`.
#}
{% set header_is_overlay = is_page('index') %}
{% set header_logo = theme.settings.get('logo_light') and header_is_overlay
    ? theme.settings.get('logo_light')
    : store.logo %}

<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">{{ trans('theme.header.skip_to_content') }}</a>

{# T-3.03 — the marquee sits ABOVE the header in the artboard, and only on Home.
   It is included here rather than registered as a home section because a
   registered section renders inside `<main>`, below the header — the wrong half
   of the page. It stays in normal flow; the header below is the thing that
   overlays the hero, and it offsets itself by this bar's height. #}
{% if header_is_overlay %}
    {% include 'components.announcement-bar' with { position: 'top' } %}
{% endif %}

{#
  T-3.05 — the sentinel, and it exists only where a state change can happen.

  On Home the header is absolutely positioned at `--header-offset`, so this
  zero-height marker sits at exactly the header's own top edge: the moment it
  leaves the viewport is the moment the header would have scrolled away.
  `partials/sticky-header.js` watches it with an IntersectionObserver and swaps
  the state. Everywhere else the header is in normal flow and CSS `sticky` pins
  it with no script and no sentinel — there is no state to change there, only a
  position to hold.

  `header_is_sticky` is upstream's own setting and it gates both paths: no
  sentinel means nothing to observe, and no `--sticky` class means nothing pins.
#}
{% set header_is_sticky = theme.settings.get('header_is_sticky', true) %}

{% if header_is_overlay and header_is_sticky %}
    <span class="store-header__sentinel" data-sticky-sentinel aria-hidden="true"></span>
{% endif %}

<header data-testid="store-header"
        data-sticky-header
        class="store-header
               {{ header_is_overlay ? 'store-header--overlay' : 'store-header--solid' }}
               {{ header_is_sticky and not header_is_overlay ? 'store-header--sticky' : '' }}">
    {# T-2.18/T-2.19 — the container carries the 16px page gutter and the bar is
       its child, so the bar's panel lands at 16..377 exactly as the export draws
       it. Same construction as `.s-block__panel`. #}
    <div class="container">
    <div class="store-header__bar">
        <div class="store-header__group store-header__group--start">
            {#
              T-3.06 — the burger is a BUTTON that opens the T-2.10 sheet.

              It was an `<a href="#mobile-menu">` with mmenu's `mburger` classes,
              **pointing at an id nothing has emitted since T-3.04 replaced this
              file** — so it navigated nowhere and the store had no menu at all.
              A control that opens an overlay is a button, not a link: a link
              promises a destination, and `href="#…"` on a control that does not
              navigate is what put this in the state it was in.
            #}
            <button type="button"
                    data-testid="store-header-mobile-toggle"
                    class="store-header__btn"
                    data-sheet-open="main-menu-sheet"
                    aria-label="{{ trans('blocks.header.main_menu') }}">
                {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'menu', size: 'xl' } %}
            </button>

            {# The search modal itself is already rendered by master.twig; this only opens it. #}
            <button type="button"
                    data-testid="store-header-search"
                    class="store-header__btn"
                    onclick="salla.event.dispatch('search::open')"
                    aria-label="{{ trans('theme.header.search') }}">
                {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'search', size: 'xl' } %}
            </button>
        </div>

        <a data-testid="store-header-logo" class="store-header__brand" href="{{ store.url }}">
            <img src="{{ header_logo|cdn(175) }}"
                 alt="{{ store.name }}"
                 width="175"
                 height="40"
                 fetchpriority="high"
                 loading="eager">
            {# The store name as the page's heading. Upstream's rule, preserved:
               h1 on the home page, h2 everywhere else, so no page ends up with two. #}
            {% if is_page('index') %}
                <h1 class="sr-only">{{ store.name }}</h1>
            {% else %}
                <h2 class="sr-only">{{ store.name }}</h2>
            {% endif %}
        </a>

        <div class="store-header__group store-header__group--end">
            <salla-cart-summary data-testid="store-header-cart" class="store-header__btn">
                <i slot="icon" class="sicon-shopping-bag" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </salla-cart-summary>

            <salla-user-menu data-testid="store-header-user-menu"
                             class="store-header__user"
                             avatar-only show-header show-trigger></salla-user-menu>
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>

    {#
      The cart count, announced.

      `salla-cart-summary` renders the badge visually and nothing tells a screen
      reader when it changes. This region is what `app.js` already updates: its
      `onUpdated` handler writes the number into every `[data-cart-count]` on the
      page, and a text change inside a live region is what triggers the
      announcement — so no new script is needed for this to work.

      The number comes LAST on purpose. "السلة: ٣" needs no plural agreement,
      where "٣ منتجات" would need six Arabic forms and `trans()` cannot select
      between them (see the note in scripts/check-locales.mjs).
    #}
    {#
      T-4.11 verified this region rather than rebuilding it, and found one thing
      short of what the note above claims. `aria-atomic` defaults to false, which
      means only the node that changed is announced — and the only node that
      changes is the number. So the region said «٣», not «السلة: ٣»: a bare digit
      with nothing to attach it to, arriving a second after a tap. Announcing the
      region whole is a single attribute and the difference between a number and
      a sentence.
    #}
    <span class="sr-only" role="status" aria-atomic="true">
        {{ trans('blocks.header.cart') }}: <span data-cart-count>{{ cart.items_count }}</span>
    </span>
</header>

{#
  T-3.06 — what the burger opens.

  IT IS THE T-2.10 SHEET, NOT A DRAWER. mmenu-light was evaluated and its bundle
  contains **zero** occurrences of `aria`, `focus`, `keydown` or `tabindex` — so
  focus is neither trapped nor returned and submenus expose no state, which is
  three of this task's four criteria failing at once with no CSS path to any of
  them. The primitive already does all three, and "RTL slide direction correct"
  stops being a question when the panel rises from the bottom edge rather than
  from a side.

  THE THREE UTILITIES ARE THE POINT OF THE FOOTER OF THIS SHEET. T-3.04 removed
  upstream's top navbar because no artboard draws it, and carried its two pieces
  of *functionality* here. This task must not close without them — a multilingual
  store with no switcher anywhere is a regression, not a simplification:

    · `salla-localization-modal show-trigger` — language and currency. `show-trigger`
      makes the component render its own opener, which is why no button is
      written here. Gated exactly as upstream gated it.
    · `salla-contacts` — the store's own contact links, without `is-header`,
      which was a layout hint for a bar that no longer exists.
    · **the store scope**, which T-3.04 did *not* carry and which was about to be
      lost in the same way. `salla-scopes` is still rendered by `master.twig`, but
      its only trigger lived in the navbar — so a store with branches could not
      open it unless the scope was configured as a mandatory popup. One button,
      dispatching the event upstream dispatched.

  UPSTREAM'S `salla-menu source="footer" topnav` IS NOT RESTORED, and that is not
  an oversight. It repeats the «روابط مهمة» column T-3.08 already renders in the
  footer of every page; the two things above were carried because they exist
  nowhere else, and this one exists somewhere else.
#}
{% set main_menu_body %}
    <custom-main-menu data-testid="store-main-menu"></custom-main-menu>

    <div class="nav-menu__utilities">
        {% if store.settings.is_multilingual or store.settings.currencies_enabled %}
            <salla-localization-modal data-testid="store-menu-localization" show-trigger></salla-localization-modal>
        {% endif %}

        {% if store.scope %}
            <button type="button"
                    class="btn btn--neutral"
                    onclick="salla.event.dispatch('scopes::open', {'mode': 'default'})">
                {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'location' } only %}
                <span class="btn__label">{{ store.scope.name }}</span>
            </button>
        {% endif %}

        <salla-contacts data-testid="store-menu-contacts"></salla-contacts>
    </div>
{% endset %}

{% include 'components.ui.bottom-sheet' with {
    id:    'main-menu-sheet',
    title: trans('blocks.header.main_menu'),
    body:  main_menu_body
} only %}
